  data:  # e7b8
    kind: work_item  # e7b8
    title: "Java/Kotlin/js_ts analyzers and the core inheritance linker (C#, C++, Go, Groovy, Scala, PHP) bind a base imported from an external package, or written qualified, to an in-repo class of the same simple name (non-Python sibling of WI-ratid)"  # e7b8
    status: todo_hard  # e7b8
    priority: 2  # e7b8
    parent:  # e7b8
    tags:  # e7b8
    - analysis_quality  # e7b8
    - dispatch  # e7b8
    - java  # e7b8
    - kotlin  # e7b8
    - javascript  # e7b8
    - csharp  # e7b8
    isbefore: []  # e7b8
    duplicate_of: []  # e7b8
    not_duplicate_of: []  # e7b8
    pr_ref:  # e7b8
    description: "Sibling-language counterpart of WI-ratid-mokat-fifon-hiros-nazun-bozim-mojak-jasin (Python, fixed on branch jgstern-agent/fix/ratid). A base class named through an import of an EXTERNAL package, or written fully qualified, binds to an unrelated in-repo class that shares its simple name. Ruby is filed separately as WI-kazut-zomas-lujoj-balug-puvif-pibum-paluz-sikum.\n\nTwo mechanisms, both by name only:\n(A) ANALYZER: `_resolve_base_class_java` (java.py ~2124), `_resolve_base_class_kotlin` (kotlin.py ~2154), `_resolve_base_class_js` (js_ts.py ~2742) return the ONLY candidate when there is exactly one; the file's imports break ties between 2+ candidates only. So `import junit.framework.TestCase; class T extends TestCase` (Java), `import androidx.lifecycle.ViewModel; class M : ViewModel()` (Kotlin), `import {Component} from 'react'; class A extends Component` and `class A extends React.Component` (js_ts strips to the last segment, js_ts.py ~2893-2907) all get a RESOLVED extends edge to an in-repo `TestCase` / `ViewModel` / `Component`. The core linker then skips the pair (existing_pairs), so fixing only the linker does not help.\n(B) CORE LINKER (`inheritance.py::_create_inheritance_edges`): retries the last segment after `.` / `::` with no import context. Reached for C# (`class E : System.Exception`, and bare `using System; class E : Exception`), C++ (`class E : public std::exception`), Java qualified GENERIC bases (`extends java.util.ArrayList<String>`), Go interface assertions (`var _ io.Writer = &X{}`; Go embeds are already stripped to the last segment in go.py ~1086), and bare imported bases in Groovy / Scala / PHP (`use Illuminate\\...\\Model; class User extends Model`).\n\nEvidence: code reading by a sweep sub-agent on 2026-10-03 (file:line above, grammar AST shape probed for Kotlin/Swift/Java/Groovy/Scala/PHP/C#/C++/ObjC with installed tree-sitter grammars). NOT reproduced end-to-end and NOT measured on any corpus repo. Consequence when it fires: wrong extends edge -> wrong inherited-method resolution in the MRO walkers, and a possible cycle (Java/Ruby/Groovy walkers use visited sets and do not refuse; the Python C3 refusal is WI-ratid's sibling item).\n\nFix direction (Python's, WI-ratid): resolve the base expression's root through the file's imports first; if the import names an out-of-tree package, emit an unresolved external edge with an ExternalRef; the core linker already skips a base an analyzer classified that way (WI-ratid's `analyzer_external_bases`). Languages with no import model (Apex, ObjC, Swift module-wide imports) are out of scope.\n\nSeparate bugs found by the same sweep, NOT this item: Kotlin and Swift keep the FIRST segment of a qualified base (`java.io.Serializable` -> `java`; kotlin.py ~937, swift.py ~231); PHP qualified bases (`\\Foo\\Bar`) are dropped entirely because the linker splits only on `.`/`::` and the external-name guard rejects backslashes (inheritance.py `_CLEAN_IDENT`)."  # e7b8
    fields: {}  # e7b8
- op: discuss  # 4439
  at: '2026-10-18T22:48:58Z'  # 4439
  by: agent  # 4439
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4439
  clock: 2  # 4439
  nonce: '4439'  # 4439
  message: "ANALYZER HALF (mechanism A) DONE in PR #1719 (dev a6f6987b8d). New hypergumbo_lang_mainstream.import_bound_bases: Java and Kotlin record each class's package-qualified qualified_name, so an explicitly imported base whose FQN no in-repo candidate has is EXTERNAL; _resolve_base_class_java/_kotlin return None for it and the analyzer emits an unresolved extends/implements edge with ExternalRef (module_path = package), which the core linker's WI-ratid guard then leaves alone. A candidate with no qualified_name, or a base not explicitly imported (same package, java.lang, wildcard import), keeps the old name resolution (bias: a wrong in-tree verdict only keeps the old behaviour). js_ts: no qualified names, so the import SPECIFIER decides on positive evidence only -- a Node core module (or node: prefix), or a registry package declared in the importing package.json (or an ancestor's) that no in-repo package.json is named; workspace packages (workspace:/file:/link:/portal: specs, or an in-repo package name) and undeclared bare specifiers such as tsconfig aliases (@/models) keep the old resolution. LIVE REPRO on dev a6f6987b8d (hypergumbo run; in-repo org.acme.TestCase + 'import junit.framework.TestCase; class T extends TestCase'; package.json dependencies react + in-repo Component + \"import { Component } from 'react'; class A extends Component\"): T extends -> java:junit.framework:0-0:TestCase:external_symbol, A extends -> typescript:react:0-0:Component:external_symbol (before: both resolved to the in-repo namesake). Tests: hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_import_bound_external_bases.py (Java extends+implements, Kotlin, JS named/default-qualified/Node builtin, in-repo controls incl. workspace and alias, end-to-end core-linker non-rebind). REMAINING: mechanism B in the core linker (qualified bases: C# System.Exception, C++ std::exception, Java qualified generics, Go io.Writer) -- next PR; plan: a qualified base binds an in-repo candidate only when the candidate's qualified_name is the base or ends with it, which needs cpp classes to record qualified_name (they record none today). Bare imported bases in C# / Groovy / Scala / PHP need per-language import context the core linker lacks."  # 4439
- op: discuss  # addc
  at: '2026-10-18T23:47:51Z'  # addc
  by: agent  # addc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # addc
  clock: 3  # addc
  nonce: addc  # addc
  message: "LINKER HALF (mechanism B, qualified bases) DONE in PR #1720 (dev 8001c9f1da). inheritance._qualifier_fit: a qualified base's last segment binds only candidates whose qualified_name fits the written base (either ends with the other on a segment boundary -- C#/Java/Kotlin/Go/C++ record namespace-qualified names, Python the in-module qualname); candidates with no qualified_name keep the name binding; when every candidate records one and none fits, _qualified_external_edge emits an unresolved extends edge with the written qualifier as module (ExternalRef). cpp class/struct symbols now record qualified_name = namespace chain + name. LIVE REPRO on dev 8001c9f1da (hypergumbo run): C# 'namespace MyApp.Errors { class Exception }' + 'class E : System.Exception' + 'class F : Errors.Exception' -> E extends csharp:System:0-0:Exception:external_symbol, F extends the in-repo Exception; C++ 'namespace mylib { class exception }' + 'class CE : public std::exception' + 'class CF : public mylib::exception' -> CE extends cpp:std:0-0:exception:external_symbol, CF extends the in-repo exception (before: E and CE bound the in-repo namesakes). Tests: test_inheritance_linker.py::TestQualifiedBaseMustMatchItsQualifier (C#, Go, Java generic, unqualified-candidate control) and ::test_cpp_std_exception_is_not_the_in_repo_namesake (end to end). Caught by the full suite and fixed before merge: Python qualified_name is module-relative, so a one-directional fit declared pkg.testcases.TestCase external. STILL OPEN under this item: a BARE base imported through a namespace/package import -- C# 'using System; class E : Exception', PHP 'use ...\\\\Model; class User extends Model', Groovy/Scala imports. Next PR. Kotlin/Swift first-segment bug is WI-jipij (separate). PHP backslash-qualified bases dropped by the linker (_CLEAN_IDENT) is not filed yet."  # addc
