  message: "DONE across four PRs: #1719 (analyzer half: Java/Kotlin/JS-TS import-bound bases), #1720 (core linker: qualified bases must fit their qualifier; cpp classes record namespace-qualified names), #1721 (bare bases bound through namespace/package imports: analyzers record meta base_class_imports for PHP use, Groovy/Scala single-type imports and C# using aliases, and meta visible_namespaces for C#; Groovy/Scala types record package-qualified qualified_name; PHP \\\\Foo\\\\Bar bases are split on backslash instead of being dropped). FINAL LIVE REPRO on dev 62ac07d6a3 (hypergumbo run on one mixed fixture with an in-repo namesake for every base): PHP 'use Illuminate\\\\Database\\\\Eloquent\\\\Model; class User extends Model' -> php:Illuminate\\\\Database\\\\Eloquent:0-0:Model:external_symbol; Groovy 'import groovy.lang.Script' -> groovy:groovy.lang:0-0:Script:external_symbol; Scala 'import akka.actor.Actor' -> scala:akka.actor:0-0:Actor:external_symbol; C# 'using System; namespace MyApp { class CE : Exception }' -> csharp:external:0-0:Exception:external_symbol while 'using MyApp.Errors; ... class CF : Exception' -> the in-repo Exception; Java 'import junit.framework.TestCase' -> java:junit.framework:0-0:TestCase:external_symbol and 'extends java.util.ArrayList<String>' -> java:java.util:0-0:ArrayList:external_symbol. Before WI-pivap every one of these bound the in-repo namesake. Tests: hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_import_bound_external_bases.py (all languages, end to end, with in-repo controls incl. aliases, workspace packages, path aliases, enclosing namespaces, using static) and test_inheritance_linker.py (TestQualifiedBaseMustMatchItsQualifier, TestBareImportedBases). Bias throughout: a candidate with no qualified_name, or no positive evidence of an external package, keeps the old name binding. NOT in scope and still open: WI-jipij (Kotlin/Swift keep the FIRST segment of a qualified base). Languages with no import model (Apex, ObjC, Swift module-wide imports) are out of scope as the item stated. Not measured on a corpus repo."  # 829f
